1 | devops | Fix PR 2829 on branch feat/ac-w2a-iris-scaffold per the two round-one comments on issue 2340 whose first lines read CRITIC W2A IRIS SCAFFOLD and SECURITY W2A IRIS SCAFFOLD. READ BOTH IN FULL FIRST. One commit per item. SCOPE MAP FIRST: in scripts/hooks/scope-check.sh give the Go code of the standalone services an owner: go-backend gets services/iris/ and services/hermes/ in addition to apps/api/; narrow the devops grant on services/ to the infrastructure files that motivated it (Dockerfile, .dockerignore, .env.example, README.md, and the deploy workflow which is already under .github) and make the comment describe exactly what the code enforces (security MEDIUM three). CRITIC B1: add the stdlib-only services/iris/cmd/iris/main_test.go the critic supplied verbatim, and show it red on the mutation and green on the branch. CRITIC B2: the isolation gate header claims services never touch the database; add the third check (no database driver import: pgx, database/sql, lib/pq, sqlc generated packages) to scripts/check-service-isolation.sh with a throwaway proof that it goes red. CRITIC F1 and SECURITY MEDIUM one: the documented whole-channel kill switch does not stop traffic; replace it in docs/operations/env-vars-iris.md and the same inherited text in docs/operations/env-vars-hermes.md with a command that denies ingress (remove the allUsers run.invoker binding, or set ingress internal), with the restore command beside it, and document the per-host kill switch env var from the edge as the D4-respecting option once the edge lands. CRITIC F2: the first prod revision must not report environment development; pass ENVIRONMENT production in deploy-iris.yml the way deploy-hermes does. CRITIC F3: add the Iris rows to CLAUDE.md (agent table note and Where to find X). CRITIC F4: fix the dangling reference to check-hermes-isolation.sh in apps/api/internal/apievent/synthetic_enumeration_test.go (one word; this file is outside your scope, so if the hook refuses, leave a one-line note in the handoff and wave 2 does it). SECURITY MEDIUM two: bump the production base image in services/iris/Dockerfile to a supported Alpine, and file one issue for apps/api and services/hermes carrying the same pin, referenced in the commit. SECURITY LOWs: add services/iris/.dockerignore; Cache-Control no-store on the health response is wave 2 (Go); remove the secret the bootstrap attaches that no code reads, or note it as reserved for the edge in the env doc; state the rate-limit posture for a single pinned instance in env-vars-iris.md. VERIFY: go test in services/iris with the race flag, the isolation gate green for both services and red on the two throwaway proofs, make check-ci-wiring, make check-prd-index if docs/prd changed; paste real exit codes. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash anywhere, no AI tool or vendor name, no Co-Authored-By trailer. Push to the same branch, keep the PR a draft. | feat/ac-w2a-iris-scaffold

2 | go-backend | On branch feat/ac-w2a-iris-scaffold after wave 1 (which gives you write scope on services/iris), build the edge of the connector, no tools yet, and close the wave-level blocker W1 from the critic comment CRITIC W2A IRIS SCAFFOLD on issue 2340. READ FIRST docs/prd/pages/assistant-channel.md sections 1, 3.0 to 3.2, 3.3.8, 3.4 and 6, the W1-D authorization server on main (apps/api/internal/handler/assistant_oauth.go, service/assistant_auth.go, middleware/auth.go: the assistant scope, the binding_id claim, the per-binding liveness check), the MCP specification 2025-11-25 sections on streamable HTTP transport, authorization, protected resource metadata and tool annotations (fetch and cite by section in code comments), and the critic W1 section with its supplied failing test. Deliver in services/iris unless stated: ONE, W1 in apps/api: every 401 and the audience 403 on the assistant paths carry a WWW-Authenticate Bearer challenge with resource_metadata pointing at the protected resource metadata document and the scope list, so both hosts can find the authorization server; add the critic test apps/api/internal/middleware/assistant_challenge_test.go verbatim and make it green. TWO, a streamable HTTP MCP endpoint in iris that on a missing or invalid bearer answers 401 with the same challenge, and serves /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource on the iris origin naming the API as the authorization server, exactly as section 6 requires. THREE, bearer validation: verify the assistant access token the way the API middleware does, sharing no code with apps/api/internal (copy the minimal verification or call an existing API verification endpoint; state which and why in the README), reject any token without the assistant scope, forward binding_id and user on every downstream call. FOUR, the tool manifest listing the seven Wave 2 tool names from section 3.3 with titles, descriptions and annotations (readOnlyHint true for the six read tools, false for update_trip, destructiveHint false, openWorldHint false), the two Wave 3 names answering not_available per section 3.3.8, and a stub per tool returning not_available in the section 3.4 error shape. FIVE, the per-host kill switch: an env var listing disabled client ids; a disabled host gets not_available with a fixed sentence, logged once per binding per hour. SIX, structured logging per call with binding_id, client_id, tool name, outcome and duration, never an argument or result payload, per docs/operations/provider-refusal-logging.md; Cache-Control no-store on the health and well-known responses. VERIFY: go test ./... with the race flag in services/iris and in apps/api, tests for the 401 shape, the scope rejection, the manifest annotations and the kill switch; real exit codes pasted in the PR body. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash anywhere, no AI tool or vendor name in code comments, commit or PR text, no Co-Authored-By trailer. Push to the same branch, keep the PR a draft. | feat/ac-w2a-iris-scaffold

3 | backend-critic | READ-ONLY RE-REVIEW of PR 2829 on branch feat/ac-w2a-iris-scaffold after the fix waves. No commits, no push, no review, no labels, no edits; tmp writes only. Record head SHA at start and at report. Grade B1, B2, F1 to F4 and W1 from your round-one comment CLEARED or STILL OPEN with proof (re-run your mutation and the throwaway proofs, run your challenge test). Then the edge questions: is the service a boundary and nothing else (any supplier, payment or ranking import is a BLOCK); does the 401 carry resource_metadata and does the metadata name the API issuer; is a token without the assistant scope rejected before any downstream call; do the manifest annotations match section 6; does the kill switch cut one host and not the other; did the scope-map change give go-backend exactly the two service trees and narrow devops to infrastructure files. Write failing tests for anything that fails and paste results. Post ONE comment on issue 2340 whose first line reads CRITIC W2A IRIS SCAFFOLD ROUND 2 with SAFE-TO-MERGE or BLOCK-FIX and citations. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash, no AI tool or vendor name. | feat/ac-w2a-iris-scaffold

